infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title The quorum knob (N=3): one store, three operating points
  desc R + W > N forces the read set to overlap the write set
  lists
    - label W=2, R=2 — balanced default
      desc Both quorums need 2 of 3 nodes; a read always sees the latest acknowledged write — the common all-round setting
    - label W=1, R=3 — fast writes
      desc One node acks a write, so a put survives if any single node is up; reads pay for it by polling all 3 replicas
    - label W=3, R=1 — durable writes, fast reads
      desc Every replica must ack, so reads need just 1 node; but a write fails or stalls the moment any node is down
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
